            'cover' => 'aetherfall/screenshots/fortress.jpg',
            'body' => '<p>Aetherfall is a complete <strong>Aion 4.8 NA repack</strong> you download and run yourself. It includes the client, game services, Java and MariaDB. Play on your own machine or host a shared world for friends. See <a href="/info#repack-features">Repack Features</a> for the full overview.</p><h2>Solo, co-op and companion parties</h2><p>Recruit offline characters from your account or temporary companions. Set roles, skills, equipment, formations and spacing, then use Follow, Stay, Attack and Passive orders. Eligible parties can expand into native alliances. Owned alts retain their class, level, gear and progress, and can share eligible quest completions and normal rewards. Multiple clients are supported with a separate game account for each session.</p><h2>Party tactics and supplies</h2><p>Pull enemies back to the party, mark kill targets and reserve crowd-control targets. Class-specific healing, buffs, recovery and pet support use learned skills, resources and cooldowns. Choose earned equipment, starter gear for empty slots or optional generated upgrades. Native trade, mail, warehouse and eligible legion-warehouse services keep their normal requirements and permissions.</p><h2>Independent world bots</h2><p>World bots choose their own questing, combat, gathering, crafting and town activities. Their identities and progress persist across population rotation. Configure population, faction balance, levels and activity. Native legions, configurable faction PvP and travel through real open rifts add activity beyond your own party.</p><h2>Trade, appearances and progression</h2><p>Central Market offers buying, selling, history and collection storage. Wardrobe and the in-game Cash Shop have dedicated menus. Aetherpass brings missions and reward tracks into the game, while Journey includes companion starting choices. Account Fame and Boons provide progression and benefit details. These game features are separate from website Donation Coins.</p><h2>Storage and loot</h2><p>The unified inventory has 189 base slots and supported expansion up to 288. Character Warehouse has 360 slots and Account Warehouse has 540, with search, filtering and scrollable layouts. Earned expansions are retained. Need / Greed / Pass panels show item icons, tooltips, countdowns and party choices. Companion rolls consider usability and role, with normal ownership and capacity checks.</p><h2>Interface and Stigma controls</h2><p>Arrange windows with Move UI, save positions, adjust transparency, choose tooltip placement and customise chat backdrops, themes and the companion toolbar. Quest-target progress and item comparisons remain available. Profile Stigma controls support eligible equip and removal, and an Upgrade button opens the existing charging window. Slots, costs, materials and success rules remain unchanged.</p><h2>Quests, encounters and difficulty</h2><p>The Unbroken Field adds sixteen Verteron quests. Targeted repairs cover Verteron, Theobomos Lab, Adma Stronghold and Steel Rake. Open-world HP and damage can scale with nearby parties or alliances while preserving native XP; instances follow separate rules. Quest, navigation and encounter coverage continue to be developed.</p><h2>Client and installation tools</h2><p>The graphical launcher includes graphics controls, Direct3D 9/Vulkan selection, optional Remember Login and recovery support. HD world textures are a separate option. Setup supports resumable downloads, local archives, Server Control and cumulative updates that retain accounts, characters, progress and customised settings.</p><p>The companion website is installed separately and connects to the game installation you configure. <a href="/start">Use the installation checklist</a>, <a href="/guides">browse the guides</a> or <a href="/download">get the repack</a>.</p>',
